---
import BlockLayout from '../layouts/BlockLayout.astro';
const built = new Date().toISOString();
---
<BlockLayout
  title="Drum Live — hear who else is drumming right now"
  description="A live drum artifact. Open it on a phone or a laptop. Tap the four pads. You'll hear every other person who has the same page open at the same moment, in their own color. Built on the PointCast drum bus."
  image="/images/og-drum.png"
>
  <main class="dl" id="dl" data-built={built}>
    <header class="dl__hero">
      <div class="dl__hero-row">
        <span class="dl__live-chip" id="dl-live-chip">
          <span class="dl__live-dot"></span>
          <span class="dl__live-text">LIVE</span>
        </span>
        <span class="dl__here" id="dl-here-text">listening for others…</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="dl__title">Hear the room.</h1>
      <p class="dl__sub">Tap the four pads. Every other person who has this page open right now will hear your taps in your color, and you'll hear theirs in theirs. It's the same drum bus the rest of PointCast runs on. Latency is about two seconds. Send this link to a friend and you'll be in the same room.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="dl__pads" id="dl-pads">
      <button class="dl__pad dl__pad--low" data-seed="20" type="button" aria-label="Low drum">
        <span class="dl__pad-label">LOW</span>
        <span class="dl__pad-pitch">70Hz</span>
        <span class="dl__pad-ring"></span>
      </button>
      <button class="dl__pad dl__pad--mid" data-seed="42" type="button" aria-label="Mid drum">
        <span class="dl__pad-label">MID</span>
        <span class="dl__pad-pitch">120Hz</span>
        <span class="dl__pad-ring"></span>
      </button>
      <button class="dl__pad dl__pad--high" data-seed="101" type="button" aria-label="High drum">
        <span class="dl__pad-label">HIGH</span>
        <span class="dl__pad-pitch">200Hz</span>
        <span class="dl__pad-ring"></span>
      </button>
      <button class="dl__pad dl__pad--bell" data-seed="333" type="button" aria-label="Bell">
        <span class="dl__pad-label">BELL</span>
        <span class="dl__pad-pitch">600Hz</span>
        <span class="dl__pad-ring"></span>
      </button>
    </section>

    <section class="dl__activity">
      <p class="dl__activity-label">RECENT TAPS</p>
      <div class="dl__activity-row" id="dl-activity-row"></div>
      <p class="dl__activity-hint" id="dl-activity-hint">Your taps appear in flame. Others appear in their own color, hashed from their session.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="dl__panel">
      <button class="dl__toggle" id="dl-toggle-others" aria-pressed="true">
        <span class="dl__toggle-dot"></span>
        <span class="dl__toggle-text">Hear others</span>
      </button>
      <a class="dl__share" id="dl-share" href="#">
        <span class="dl__share-icon">↗</span>
        <span class="dl__share-text">Copy share link</span>
      </a>
      <span class="dl__share-status" id="dl-share-status"></span>
    </section>

    <section class="dl__about">
      <h2 class="dl__about-h">How this works</h2>
      <p>When you tap a pad your browser POSTs a small JSON event (<code>&#123;type:'drum',seed,sessionId&#125;</code>) to <code>/api/sounds</code>. The server hashes your session into a 10-character pid and stores the event in a rolling 50-event KV buffer with a 30-second age cap.</p>
      <p>This page polls <code>/api/sounds?since=&lt;lastT&gt;</code> every ~1.8 seconds. Any event whose pid isn't yours fires the corresponding drum locally — slightly quieter than your own taps, slightly pitched up or down by a hash of the sender's pid so two strangers don't sound identical. The activity row at the bottom paints a small dot per recent tap in each pid's color.</p>
      <p>It's the same bus the rest of PointCast runs on. Tap a noun on the home page, an emoji on a profile, a drum on <a href="/drum-v2">/drum-v2</a>, or here — every cast surface (<a href="/drum-tv">/drum-tv</a>, /drum-radio, /drum-viz) reads the same buffer.</p>
      <p>Why latency is ~2 seconds: it's KV + polling, not WebSockets or Durable Objects. The trade is "good enough for room vibes" against operational complexity. If three of you are in the same room with your phones, the loop closes — you can play call-and-response slowly across the latency.</p>
      <p>Send this link to a friend in iMessage. The page renders a rich preview, and when they tap through both of you are in the same room.</p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <style is:global>
    :root {
      --dl-ink: #0a1230;
      --dl-ink-deep: #060a1c;
      --dl-flame: #f6c15e;
      --dl-flame-deep: #d68f2c;
      --dl-coral: #ff6b8a;
      --dl-mint: #8aeac0;
      --dl-sky: #7ac8ed;
      --dl-mauve: #c9a8ef;
      --dl-cream: #f4e7c8;
      --dl-cream-dim: #b8aa84;
      --dl-cream-dimmer: #7a7058;
    }

    body:has(.dl) {
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at 20% 0%, #2a1e58 0%, transparent 45%),
        radial-gradient(circle at 80% 100%, #1a2e58 0%, transparent 50%),
        var(--dl-ink);
      color: var(--dl-cream);
      font-family: 'Inter', -apple-system, system-ui, sans-serif;
      min-height: 100vh;
    }

    .dl {
      max-width: 920px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 32px 20px 48px;
    }

    /* HERO */
    .dl__hero {
      max-width: 720px;
      margin: 0 auto 32px;
    }
    .dl__hero-row {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 12px;
      margin-bottom: 18px;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }
    .dl__live-chip {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 6px;
      padding: 4px 10px;
      border-radius: 12px;
      background: rgba(255,107,138,0.18);
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,107,138,0.42);
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
      font-size: 10px;
      letter-spacing: 0.16em;
      color: var(--dl-coral);
    }
    .dl__live-dot {
      width: 7px; height: 7px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: var(--dl-coral);
      box-shadow: 0 0 8px rgba(255,107,138,0.7);
      animation: dlLiveBlink 1.4s ease-in-out infinite;
    }
    @keyframes dlLiveBlink {
      0%, 100% { opacity: 1; }
      50% { opacity: 0.35; }
    }
    .dl__here {
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: 11px;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      color: var(--dl-cream-dim);
    }
    .dl__here strong {
      color: var(--dl-flame);
      font-weight: 600;
    }
    .dl__title {
      font-family: 'Inter Tight', sans-serif;
      font-weight: 800;
      font-size: clamp(40px, 7vw, 72px);
      letter-spacing: -0.03em;
      line-height: 0.98;
      margin: 0 0 14px;
      color: var(--dl-cream);
      text-shadow: 0 4px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
    }
    .dl__sub {
      font-size: 16px;
      line-height: 1.55;
      color: var(--dl-cream-dim);
      margin: 0;
    }

    /* PADS */
    .dl__pads {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
      gap: 12px;
      margin-bottom: 22px;
    }
    @media (max-width: 600px) {
      .dl__pads { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
    }
    .dl__pad {
      position: relative;
      aspect-ratio: 1;
      border-radius: 20px;
      border: 0;
      padding: 0;
      cursor: pointer;
      transition: transform 80ms ease, box-shadow 200ms ease;
      box-shadow:
        inset 0 -8px 14px rgba(0,0,0,0.4),
        inset 0 6px 10px rgba(255,255,255,0.18),
        0 8px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      gap: 4px;
      overflow: hidden;
      touch-action: manipulation;
      user-select: none;
      -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent;
    }
    .dl__pad:active { transform: scale(0.96) translateY(2px); }
    .dl__pad--low  { background: linear-gradient(160deg, #f4a050 0%, #8a4218 100%); color: #2a1a08; }
    .dl__pad--mid  { background: linear-gradient(160deg, #ff8a9a 0%, #c43048 100%); color: #2a0810; }
    .dl__pad--high { background: linear-gradient(160deg, #c9a8ef 0%, #5a3a8c 100%); color: #1a0a30; }
    .dl__pad--bell { background: linear-gradient(160deg, #8aeac0 0%, #2a8a68 100%); color: #0a2a18; }
    .dl__pad-label {
      font-family: 'Inter Tight', sans-serif;
      font-weight: 800;
      font-size: clamp(20px, 4vw, 28px);
      letter-spacing: 0.02em;
      text-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.32);
      position: relative;
      z-index: 2;
    }
    .dl__pad-pitch {
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: 11px;
      letter-spacing: 0.14em;
      opacity: 0.72;
      text-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);
      position: relative;
      z-index: 2;
    }
    .dl__pad-ring {
      position: absolute;
      inset: 8%;
      border-radius: 50%;
      border: 2px solid currentColor;
      opacity: 0;
      transform: scale(0.9);
      transition: opacity 80ms ease, transform 80ms ease;
      pointer-events: none;
    }
    .dl__pad--struck .dl__pad-ring {
      animation: dlRing 800ms ease-out;
    }
    @keyframes dlRing {
      0% { opacity: 0.7; transform: scale(0.8); }
      100% { opacity: 0; transform: scale(1.4); }
    }
    .dl__pad--struck-other .dl__pad-ring {
      animation: dlRingOther 1200ms ease-out;
    }
    @keyframes dlRingOther {
      0% { opacity: 0.4; transform: scale(0.85); border-style: dashed; }
      100% { opacity: 0; transform: scale(1.3); border-style: dashed; }
    }

    /* ACTIVITY */
    .dl__activity {
      background: rgba(0,0,0,0.32);
      border: 1px solid rgba(246,193,94,0.16);
      border-radius: 16px;
      padding: 14px 16px;
      margin-bottom: 18px;
    }
    .dl__activity-label {
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: 10px;
      letter-spacing: 0.14em;
      color: var(--dl-cream-dimmer);
      margin: 0 0 10px;
    }
    .dl__activity-row {
      display: flex;
      gap: 6px;
      flex-wrap: nowrap;
      align-items: center;
      min-height: 28px;
      overflow: hidden;
    }
    .dl__activity-row:empty::before {
      content: 'no taps yet';
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: 11px;
      color: var(--dl-cream-dimmer);
    }
    .dl__act-dot {
      width: 22px;
      height: 22px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      flex-shrink: 0;
      animation: dlDotIn 360ms ease-out;
      box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);
      position: relative;
    }
    .dl__act-dot--self {
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px rgba(246,193,94,0.55), 0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);
    }
    @keyframes dlDotIn {
      from { transform: scale(0.4); opacity: 0; }
      to { transform: scale(1); opacity: 1; }
    }
    .dl__activity-hint {
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: 10px;
      color: var(--dl-cream-dimmer);
      margin: 10px 0 0;
    }

    /* PANEL */
    .dl__panel {
      display: flex;
      gap: 10px;
      align-items: center;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      margin-bottom: 28px;
    }
    .dl__toggle, .dl__share {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 8px;
      padding: 8px 14px;
      border-radius: 10px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(244,231,200,0.22);
      background: transparent;
      color: var(--dl-cream);
      cursor: pointer;
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: 11px;
      letter-spacing: 0.10em;
      text-decoration: none;
      transition: background 100ms ease;
    }
    .dl__toggle:hover, .dl__share:hover { background: rgba(244,231,200,0.08); }
    .dl__toggle-dot {
      width: 8px;
      height: 8px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: var(--dl-mint);
      box-shadow: 0 0 6px rgba(138,234,192,0.55);
    }
    .dl__toggle[aria-pressed="false"] .dl__toggle-dot {
      background: var(--dl-cream-dimmer);
      box-shadow: none;
    }
    .dl__share-icon {
      font-size: 13px;
      color: var(--dl-flame);
    }
    .dl__share-status {
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: 11px;
      color: var(--dl-mint);
    }

    /* ABOUT */
    .dl__about {
      max-width: 720px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding-top: 24px;
      border-top: 1px solid rgba(244,231,200,0.12);
    }
    .dl__about-h {
      font-family: 'Inter Tight', sans-serif;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 20px;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      color: var(--dl-cream);
      margin: 0 0 12px;
    }
    .dl__about p {
      font-size: 14px;
      line-height: 1.6;
      color: var(--dl-cream-dim);
      margin: 0 0 12px;
    }
    .dl__about code {
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: 12px;
      padding: 1px 6px;
      border-radius: 4px;
      background: rgba(244,231,200,0.08);
      color: var(--dl-flame);
    }
    .dl__about a {
      color: var(--dl-flame);
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
      text-underline-offset: 3px;
    }
  </style>

  <script>
    import { createAudioScheduler } from '../lib/audio-scheduler';

    // ---- session + pid (matches server: sha256(sessionId).slice(0, 10)) ----
    let SESSION_ID = '';
    let MY_PID = '';
    let lastT = 0;
    let hearOthers = true;
    let pollTimer: number | null = null;

    // Map pid → { color, lastSeen } for "who's here" + recent activity colors
    const pidColors = new Map();

    // Color palette for unknown pids (deterministic by pid hash)
    const PALETTE = [
      '#ff6b8a', '#8aeac0', '#7ac8ed', '#c9a8ef',
      '#f4a050', '#ffd56b', '#ff9bd4', '#6be5d4',
      '#a8d870', '#e89070', '#b894e8', '#70c0d8',
    ];

    function pidColor(pid: string): string {
      if (pid === MY_PID) return '#f6c15e';
      // Simple hash → palette index
      let h = 0;
      for (let i = 0; i < pid.length; i++) h = (h * 31 + pid.charCodeAt(i)) | 0;
      return PALETTE[Math.abs(h) % PALETTE.length];
    }

    async function sha256Hex(input: string) {
      const buf = new TextEncoder().encode(input);
      const hash = await crypto.subtle.digest('SHA-256', buf);
      return Array.from(new Uint8Array(hash))
        .map((b) => b.toString(16).padStart(2, '0'))
        .join('');
    }

    function getOrCreateSession(): string {
      try {
        let sid = localStorage.getItem('pc-drum-live-session');
        if (!sid) {
          sid = `dl-${Date.now()}-${Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 10)}`;
          localStorage.setItem('pc-drum-live-session', sid);
        }
        return sid;
      } catch {
        return `dl-${Date.now()}-${Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 10)}`;
      }
    }

    // ---- audio ----
    let ctx: AudioContext | null = null;
    let scheduler: ReturnType<typeof createAudioScheduler> | null = null;
    let masterGain: GainNode | null = null;

    function ensureCtx() {
      if (ctx) return;
      ctx = new (window.AudioContext || (window as any).webkitAudioContext)();
      scheduler = createAudioScheduler(ctx);
      masterGain = ctx.createGain();
      masterGain.gain.value = 0.55;
      masterGain.connect(ctx.destination);
    }

    type DrumSpec = { fundamental: number; tail: number; kind: 'thump' | 'bell' };
    const DRUM_SPECS: { [seed: number]: DrumSpec } = {
      20:  { fundamental: 70,  tail: 0.45, kind: 'thump' },
      42:  { fundamental: 120, tail: 0.42, kind: 'thump' },
      101: { fundamental: 200, tail: 0.42, kind: 'thump' },
      333: { fundamental: 600, tail: 2.6,  kind: 'bell' },
    };

    function playDrum(seed: number, isSelf: boolean, pid: string) {
      ensureCtx();
      if (!ctx || !scheduler || !masterGain) return;
      if (ctx.state === 'suspended') ctx.resume();
      const spec = DRUM_SPECS[seed] || DRUM_SPECS[42];
      const t = ctx.currentTime + 0.005;
      // Pitch-shift others by a pid-hash so each player sounds slightly distinct
      let pidShiftSemitones = 0;
      if (!isSelf) {
        let h = 0;
        for (let i = 0; i < pid.length; i++) h = (h * 31 + pid.charCodeAt(i)) | 0;
        // Range -4..+4 semitones
        pidShiftSemitones = ((Math.abs(h) % 9) - 4);
      }
      const pitchMul = Math.pow(2, pidShiftSemitones / 12);
      const fund = spec.fundamental * pitchMul;
      const vel = isSelf ? 1.0 : 0.6;

      if (spec.kind === 'thump') {
        const osc = ctx.createOscillator();
        const g = ctx.createGain();
        osc.type = 'sine';
        osc.frequency.setValueAtTime(fund, t);
        osc.frequency.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(fund * 0.5, t + 0.15);
        g.gain.setValueAtTime(0.0001, t);
        g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.55 * vel, t + 0.006);
        g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t + spec.tail);
        osc.connect(g).connect(masterGain);
        scheduler.trackSource(osc);
        osc.start(t);
        osc.stop(t + spec.tail + 0.05);
      } else {
        // Bell: 3 sine partials
        const partials = [
          { freq: fund,      gain: 0.32, decay: spec.tail },
          { freq: fund * 2,  gain: 0.18, decay: spec.tail * 0.7 },
          { freq: fund * 4,  gain: 0.06, decay: spec.tail * 0.4 },
        ];
        for (const p of partials) {
          const osc = ctx.createOscillator();
          const g = ctx.createGain();
          osc.type = 'sine';
          osc.frequency.value = p.freq;
          g.gain.setValueAtTime(0.0001, t);
          g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(p.gain * vel, t + 0.006);
          g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t + p.decay);
          osc.connect(g).connect(masterGain);
          scheduler.trackSource(osc);
          osc.start(t);
          osc.stop(t + p.decay + 0.1);
        }
      }
    }

    // ---- visual feedback ----
    function flashPad(seed: number, isSelf: boolean) {
      const pad = document.querySelector(`.dl__pad[data-seed="${seed}"]`);
      if (!pad) return;
      pad.classList.remove('dl__pad--struck', 'dl__pad--struck-other');
      (pad as any).offsetHeight;
      pad.classList.add(isSelf ? 'dl__pad--struck' : 'dl__pad--struck-other');
      setTimeout(() => pad.classList.remove('dl__pad--struck', 'dl__pad--struck-other'), 1300);
    }

    function pushActivityDot(seed: number, pid: string, isSelf: boolean) {
      const row = document.getElementById('dl-activity-row')!;
      const dot = document.createElement('div');
      dot.className = 'dl__act-dot' + (isSelf ? ' dl__act-dot--self' : '');
      dot.style.background = pidColor(pid);
      dot.title = isSelf ? 'you' : pid;
      row.insertBefore(dot, row.firstChild);
      // Cap at 20 dots
      while (row.children.length > 20) row.removeChild(row.lastChild!);
    }

    function refreshHereText() {
      const now = Date.now();
      // Count unique pids active in the last 25 seconds (matches server cap of 30s)
      const here = new Set();
      for (const entry of pidColors.entries()) {
        const pid = entry[0];
        const info = entry[1];
        if (now - info.lastSeen < 25000) here.add(pid);
      }
      const others = here.size - (here.has(MY_PID) ? 1 : 0);
      const el = document.getElementById('dl-here-text')!;
      if (others === 0) {
        el.innerHTML = `<span>just you so far · share the link</span>`;
      } else if (others === 1) {
        el.innerHTML = `<strong>1</strong>&nbsp;<span>other person drumming right now</span>`;
      } else {
        el.innerHTML = `<strong>${others}</strong>&nbsp;<span>others drumming right now</span>`;
      }
    }

    // ---- broadcast + poll ----
    async function broadcastTap(seed: number) {
      try {
        await fetch('/api/sounds', {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
          body: JSON.stringify({ type: 'drum', seed, sessionId: SESSION_ID }),
        });
      } catch {
        // Silent — the local tap already played, broadcast is best-effort
      }
    }

    async function pollOnce() {
      try {
        const r = await fetch(`/api/sounds?since=${lastT}`);
        if (!r.ok) return;
        const data = await r.json();
        if (!data.events || data.events.length === 0) return;
        for (const ev of data.events) {
          if (ev.type !== 'drum') continue;
          if (ev.t <= lastT) continue;
          lastT = Math.max(lastT, ev.t);
          // Record pid for "who's here" + activity colors
          pidColors.set(ev.pid, { color: pidColor(ev.pid), lastSeen: Date.now() });
          const isSelf = ev.pid === MY_PID;
          if (!isSelf && hearOthers) {
            playDrum(ev.seed, false, ev.pid);
          }
          if (!isSelf) {
            flashPad(ev.seed, false);
            pushActivityDot(ev.seed, ev.pid, false);
          }
        }
        refreshHereText();
      } catch {
        // Polling is best-effort
      }
    }

    function startPolling() {
      if (pollTimer != null) return;
      const tick = async () => {
        await pollOnce();
        pollTimer = window.setTimeout(tick, 1800);
      };
      pollTimer = window.setTimeout(tick, 800);
    }
    function stopPolling() {
      if (pollTimer != null) { clearTimeout(pollTimer); pollTimer = null; }
    }

    // ---- tap handling ----
    function handleTap(seed: number) {
      ensureCtx();
      playDrum(seed, true, MY_PID);
      flashPad(seed, true);
      pushActivityDot(seed, MY_PID, true);
      // Record self in pidColors so "here" count includes you
      pidColors.set(MY_PID, { color: '#f6c15e', lastSeen: Date.now() });
      refreshHereText();
      broadcastTap(seed);
    }

    // Map keyboard 1-4 to the four pads
    const KEY_TO_SEED: { [key: string]: number } = {
      '1': 20,
      '2': 42,
      '3': 101,
      '4': 333,
      'a': 20, 'A': 20,
      's': 42, 'S': 42,
      'd': 101, 'D': 101,
      'f': 333, 'F': 333,
    };

    async function init() {
      SESSION_ID = getOrCreateSession();
      MY_PID = (await sha256Hex(SESSION_ID)).slice(0, 10);

      document.getElementById('dl-pads')!.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => {
        const btn = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('.dl__pad');
        if (!btn) return;
        e.preventDefault();
        const seed = parseInt(btn.getAttribute('data-seed')!);
        if (!Number.isNaN(seed)) handleTap(seed);
      });

      window.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
        if (e.repeat) return;
        const tag = (e.target as HTMLElement)?.tagName?.toLowerCase();
        if (tag === 'input' || tag === 'textarea') return;
        const seed = KEY_TO_SEED[e.key];
        if (seed != null) {
          e.preventDefault();
          handleTap(seed);
        }
      });

      document.getElementById('dl-toggle-others')!.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
        const btn = e.currentTarget as HTMLButtonElement;
        hearOthers = !hearOthers;
        btn.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(hearOthers));
        btn.querySelector('.dl__toggle-text')!.textContent = hearOthers ? 'Hear others' : 'Muted';
      });

      const share = document.getElementById('dl-share')!;
      share.addEventListener('click', async (e) => {
        e.preventDefault();
        const url = location.origin + '/drum-live';
        try {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(url);
          const s = document.getElementById('dl-share-status')!;
          s.textContent = 'copied · paste in iMessage';
          setTimeout(() => { s.textContent = ''; }, 2400);
        } catch {
          const s = document.getElementById('dl-share-status')!;
          s.textContent = 'copy the URL from the address bar';
          setTimeout(() => { s.textContent = ''; }, 3000);
        }
      });

      // Visibility — pause polling when hidden to save battery
      document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', () => {
        if (document.hidden) stopPolling();
        else startPolling();
      });

      refreshHereText();
      startPolling();
    }

    if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
      document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', init);
    } else {
      init();
    }
  </script>
</BlockLayout>
